review.body:
Pinning apt to a dated Ubuntu archive snapshot looks sound. Every `apt-get update` now has `--error-on=any`, the TLS peer-check override applies only to the first build step, and the `containerd.io` pin matches its install pattern. The datasource transform now pins the exact InRelease `Date:` time instead of midnight, which settles the earlier review thread.

Three findings remain, and none of them blocks:
- the snapshot datasource reads the InRelease file over plain http;
- the schedule window can produce more than one bump a day;
- ADR 0019's new bullet contradicts that schedule.
